From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:59:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 080/342] ffmpeg plugin: decode video with at least 8 frame
 threads

Players ask for each video frame shortly before it is due, and a frame
thread's frame is only returned after the frames started after it, so
the decoder has thread_count frames under way. With one thread per core
on the ODROID-C2 (4), a frame of a 1080x1920 10 Mbit H.264 clip took
longer than those four frame times to finish; MediaPlayer showed 19.1
of its 30 frames per second, dropping late ones it had still decoded.
With 8 frame threads it shows 29.6 (HDMI capture), using 1.8 instead of
2.3 cores for decoding and 7 MB more memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVCodecDecoder.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVCodecDecoder.cpp b/src/add-ons/media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVCodecDecoder.cpp
index e361319e97..e15abb38b3 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVCodecDecoder.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/media/plugins/ffmpeg/AVCodecDecoder.cpp
@@ -28,6 +28,9 @@
 #include "Utilities.h"
 
 
+static const int kMinimumVideoThreads = 8;
+
+
 #undef TRACE
 //#define TRACE_AV_CODEC
 #ifdef TRACE_AV_CODEC
@@ -315,6 +318,13 @@ AVCodecDecoder::NegotiateOutputFormat(media_format* inOutFormat)
 	fCodecContext->err_recognition = AV_EF_CAREFUL;
 	fCodecContext->error_concealment = 3;
 	fCodecContext->thread_count = info.cpu_count;
+	if (!fIsAudio && fCodecContext->thread_count < kMinimumVideoThreads) {
+		// Frame threads decode the next frames while one is shown. Media
+		// players ask for each frame only shortly before it is due, so the
+		// frames must have been started early enough: with few cores, each
+		// frame takes longer, and more of them have to be under way.
+		fCodecContext->thread_count = kMinimumVideoThreads;
+	}
 
 	if (fIsAudio)
 		return _NegotiateAudioOutputFormat(inOutFormat);
